Faster texture uploads for the nouveau driver in devkitPro switch-mesa 20.1.0 (applies on top of glthread.patch)

On the Switch, creating a buffer object takes several calls into the GPU driver (nvmap create, address space
map, memory attribute change), which made streaming in textures cost a few hundred microseconds each.

- nvc0_transfer: take the staging memory for texture uploads from the GART slab cache (nouveau_mm) instead
  of creating and freeing a buffer object for every transfer (every mip level of every texture).
- nvc0_miptree: keep the buffer objects of freed textures in a small cache (up to 128 entries / 16 MiB) and
  reuse them for new textures of the same size and layout once the GPU is done with the old texture. The
  cache is emptied when an allocation fails and when the screen is destroyed.

